Use io, list, and string.

Define function matches_at taking text as a pointer to TcString, word as a pointer to TcString, start as an unsigned number returning a truth value:
    Let word length be length of word.
    For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to word length - 1:
        If text.data[start + i] isn't equal to word.data[i]:
            Give back false.
    Give back true.
Done.

Let text be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("barfoothefoobarman"), bytes_len("barfoothefoobarman")).
Let first word be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("foo"), bytes_len("foo")).
Let second word be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("bar"), bytes_len("bar")).
Let words be an empty list of text.
push first word to address of words.
push second word to address of words.
Let word count be count of words.
Let word length be length of address of first word.
Let text length be length of address of text.
Let total length be word count * word length.
Let last start be text length - total length.

For every offset from 0 as an unsigned number to last start:
    Let used be an empty list of whole numbers.
    For every j from 0 as an unsigned number to word count - 1:
        push 0 to address of used.
    Let all matched be true.
    For every k from 0 as an unsigned number to word count - 1:
        Let start be offset + k * word length.
        Let found be false.
        For every j from 0 as an unsigned number to word count - 1:
            Let used flag be list_get(address of used, j).
            If used flag is 0:
                Define local word as TcString.
                word = list_get(address of words, j).
                If matches_at(address of text, address of word, start):
                    list_set(address of used, j, 1).
                    Set found to true.
                    Break.
        If found is false:
            Set all matched to false.
            Break.
    If all matched is true:
        Say offset.
    list_free(address of used).

str_free(address of second word).
str_free(address of first word).
list_free(address of words).
str_free(address of text).
Return 0.
